## Overview

Turbine readings flow from each farm into one central stream and are processed once. The processed data is then split into a fast store for dashboards and a cheap archive for audits.

## Pipeline diagram

diagram pipe dir=TB title="Telemetry pipeline"
pipe: tc "Turbine Controllers" ext "On site at each farm"
pipe: edge "Edge Gateway" ext "On site at each farm"
pipe: stream "Telemetry Stream" queue focus
pipe: proc "Stream Processor" svc focus
pipe: ts "Timeseries Store" db
pipe: raw "Raw Archive" store
pipe: alert "Alerting Service" svc
pipe: dash "Operations Dashboard" ext
pipe: tc -> edge : OPC UA, 1 Hz
pipe: edge -> stream : MQTT over TLS, batched every 5 s
pipe: stream -> proc : consumer
pipe: proc -> ts : 10 s aggregates
pipe: proc -> raw : Parquet every 15 minutes
pipe: proc -> alert : threshold breach
pipe: ts -> dash : queries
pipe: group site "On site at each farm (outside the cloud account)" tc, edge
pipe: group cloud "Cloud account, eu-north-1" stream, proc, ts, raw, alert, dash

## Capacity and retention

data cap = component,size,retention; Telemetry Stream,"24 shards, 18000 messages per second at peak",—; Timeseries Store,—,"7 days in memory, 3 years on magnetic storage"; Raw Archive,—,"10 years, moved to cold storage after 90 days"

table cap

## If the uplink fails

!!! The Edge Gateway buffers only 6 hours of readings. After 6 hours without a link, the oldest readings are dropped for good.

1. The Edge Gateway buffers up to 6 hours of readings on disk.
2. When the link returns, it replays them in order.
3. If the outage lasts longer than 6 hours, the oldest readings are dropped. Treat any outage past 6 hours as data loss.
